The CSE Department will host a guest lecture by **Dr. {{lecturer_name}}** from {{lecturer_affiliation}}.

*Topic: "The Future of Quantum Computing: From Theory to Real-World Applications"*

**Date:** {{lecture_date}}
**Time:** {{lecture_time}}
**Location:** {{lecture_room}}

Dr. {{lecturer_short}} will discuss recent breakthroughs in quantum error correction, practical applications in cryptography and drug discovery, and the roadmap toward fault-tolerant quantum computers.

This lecture is open to all students and faculty. No prior quantum computing knowledge is required.

A Q&A session will follow the lecture. Refreshments will be provided.
